     <header>
       <p class="eyebrow">Feline field guide</p>
       <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
       <p class="intro">
         Quick answers for curious cat people, from purring and playtime to litter boxes and safe indoor enrichment.
       </p>
     </header>

     <main id="main-content">
       <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
               Why do cats purr?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1" hidden>
             <p>
               Cats often purr when they feel relaxed, but purring can also happen when they are seeking comfort, healing, or reassurance.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
               How much sleep do cats need?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" hidden>
             <p>
               Most adult cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats may sleep even more as their bodies grow or recover.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
               Why does my cat knead blankets?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" hidden>
             <p>
               Kneading is a comforting behavior that begins in kittenhood. Many cats keep doing it when they feel secure, sleepy, or affectionate.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
               How often should I clean the litter box?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" hidden>
             <p>
               Scoop at least once a day and fully refresh the box on a regular schedule. A clean box helps cats feel safe and reduces accidents.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
               Do indoor cats need enrichment?
               <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" hidden>
             <p>
               Yes. Puzzle feeders, climbing spots, window views, scratching posts, and short daily play sessions support healthy indoor cat behavior.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </section>
     </main>

     <footer>
       <p>For health concerns or sudden behavior changes, contact a veterinarian.</p>
     </footer>

     <script>
       const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

       questions.forEach((question) => {
         question.addEventListener("click", () => {
           const answerId = question.getAttribute("aria-controls");
           const answer = document.getElementById(answerId);
           const isExpanded = question.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

           question.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
           answer.hidden = isExpanded;
         });
       });
     </script>
   </body>
